  "description": "The CodeBoarding-action architecture follows a linear pipeline pattern designed for CI/CD environments. It orchestrates the lifecycle of architectural analysis by first executing the core engine to capture system states (Base vs. Head), then performing a structural diff to identify method-level changes. These changes are transformed into visual Mermaid.js diagrams and component-level documentation, finally culminating in the generation of interactive 'Call-to-Action' links for GitHub PR integration. The flow ensures that architectural drift is captured and visualized automatically during the development workflow.",
